{#- targum in Claude and ChatGPT (targum-internal#80, 2026-09-22).

    A public page, so §6 says it sells: lead with what the reader gets, in their words.
    "Connector" and "MCP" are our words. The word MCP appears exactly once on this page,
    in the steps, because that is what the menu they have to find is called — everything
    above it is what they get.

    **Note 2 is the whole design of this page: assume it is their first MCP install.**
    So: one block per host, each with its own steps, and nothing detected or guessed. No
    "we see you're on a Mac". A reader who is in the wrong block can see that they are,
    which is not true of a page that chose for them.

    Baked in like every public page — no script, stylesheet, font or image off the
    network (§11). It carries no script at all: there is nothing here that moves. -#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ page_language|default('en') }}">
<head>
{% include '_public_head.html.j2' %}
<style>{{ asset('landing.css') }}{{ asset('connect.css') }}</style>
{{ hebrew_face() }}
{{ chrome_face() }}
</head>
<body class="landing">
<header class="bar">
  <div class="col">
    <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="targum">
      <svg class="brand-mark" viewBox="20 12 56 72" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <rect x="20" y="12" width="22" height="62" rx="5" fill="currentColor"></rect>
        <rect x="54" y="22" width="22" height="62" rx="5" fill="var(--mark-accent)"></rect>
      </svg>
      <span>targum</span>
    </a>
  </div>
</header>

<main>
  <div class="col open">
    <h1>{{ t("connect.page.targum-in-claude-and-chatgpt", "targum in Claude and ChatGPT") }}</h1>
    <p class="lede">{{ t("connect.page.your-hebrew-your-words-and-your-mistakes", "Your Hebrew, your words and your mistakes — wherever you already ask.") }}</p>
    <p>{{ t("connect.page.ask-for-something-to-read-and-get-it", "Ask for something to read and get a text you can open, chosen for the words you already know. Ask what you were working on and hear what you actually marked, not a guess.") }}</p>
  </div>

  <section class="col">
    <h2>{{ t("connect.page.what-it-can-do", "What it can do") }}</h2>
    <ul class="can">
      <li>{{ t("connect.page.find-you-something-to-read", "Find you something to read, from the library or from a link you paste.") }}</li>
      <li>{{ t("connect.page.tell-you-what-you-were-working-on", "Tell you what you were working on, and which words you have not come back to.") }}</li>
      <li>{{ t("connect.page.show-you-a-word-in-the-sentences", "Show you a word in the sentences you actually met it in.") }}</li>
      <li>{{ t("connect.page.price-a-text-before-you-make-it", "Price a text before you make it, and hand you the link to start it.") }}</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="quiet">{{ t("connect.page.it-can-never-spend-your-hours-on-its-own", "It can never start a text on its own. It gives you a link; you press it, here.") }}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="col">
    <h2>{{ t("connect.page.adding-it", "Adding it") }}</h2>
    <p>{{ t("connect.page.paste-this-address-wherever-your-app-asks", "Paste this address wherever your app asks for one:") }}</p>
    <p class="address"><code>{{ address }}/mcp</code></p>

    <div class="host">
      <h3>{{ t("connect.page.in-claude", "In Claude") }}</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>{{ t("connect.page.claude-open-settings-then-connectors", "Open Settings, then Connectors.") }}</li>
        <li>{{ t("connect.page.claude-choose-add-custom-connector", "Choose Add custom connector.") }}</li>
        <li>{{ t("connect.page.claude-paste-the-address-above", "Paste the address above and add it.") }}</li>
        <li>{{ t("connect.page.claude-sign-in-and-choose-what-it-may-do", "Sign in to targum when it asks, and choose what it may do.") }}</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="host">
      <h3>{{ t("connect.page.in-chatgpt", "In ChatGPT") }}</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>{{ t("connect.page.chatgpt-open-settings-then-connectors", "Open Settings, then Connectors.") }}</li>
        <li>{{ t("connect.page.chatgpt-add-a-connector-and-paste", "Add a connector and paste the address above.") }}</li>
        <li>{{ t("connect.page.chatgpt-sign-in-and-choose-what-it-may-do", "Sign in to targum when it asks, and choose what it may do.") }}</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="host">
      <h3>{{ t("connect.page.in-claude-code", "In Claude Code") }}</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>{{ t("connect.page.code-run-this-in-your-terminal", "Run this in your terminal:") }}</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="address"><code>claude mcp add --transport http targum {{ address }}/mcp</code></p>
    </div>

    <p class="quiet">{{ t("connect.page.mcp-is-what-the-menu-is-called", "Some apps call this an MCP server. That is the same thing.") }}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="col">
    <h2>{{ t("connect.page.what-it-is-allowed-to-see", "What it is allowed to see") }}</h2>
    <p>{{ t("connect.page.you-choose-when-you-connect-and-you-can", "You choose when you connect, and you can take any of it back from your account whenever you like.") }}</p>
    <ul class="can">
      <li>{{ t("connect.page.the-library-and-what-is-at-a-link", "The library, and what is at a link you give it.") }}</li>
      <li>{{ t("connect.page.your-words-your-mistakes-and-how-far", "Your words, your mistakes, and how far you have got.") }}</li>
      <li>{{ t("connect.page.reading-your-hebrew-and-pricing-a-text", "Reading the Hebrew you write and pricing a text, which use your credits.") }}</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="quiet">{{ t("connect.page.what-you-say-there-stays-there", "What you say to targum here is never sent the other way.") }}</p>
  </section>

  <div class="col close">
    <h2>{{ t("connect.page.you-ll-need-a-targum-account", "You’ll need a targum account") }}</h2>
    <form class="join-form" method="post" action="/waitlist">
      <label class="field">
        <input type="email" name="email" required inputmode="email" autocapitalize="off" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="email" placeholder="{{ t("connect.page.you-example-com", "you@example.com") }}" aria-label="{{ t("connect.page.your-email", "Your email") }}">
        <button class="btn cta" type="submit">{{ t("connect.page.join-the-waitlist", "Join the waitlist") }}</button>
      </label>
      <p class="join-note">{{ t("connect.page.we-ll-email-you-when-your-turn-comes", "We’ll email you when your turn comes.") }}</p>
    </form>
  </div>
</main>

{% with signin = true %}{% include '_public_foot.html.j2' %}{% endwith %}
</body>
</html>
